<title>JAPAN: Shares related to Nissan Life fall in morning.</title>
<headline>Shares related to Nissan Life fall in morning.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in firms in which Nissan Mutual Life Insurance Co is a major shareholder declined on Friday morning after the Finance Ministry said it had ordered the insurer to halt some of its operations.</p>
<p>As of 0054 GMT, shares of Nichiro Corp had lost two yen to 301, and Hitachi Zosen Corp was down eight yen at 445. Shares in Nissan Fire &amp; Marine Insurance Co Ltd were ask-only at 480, down from Thursday's 510.</p>
<p>Firms belonging to the Nissan group, but that do not have Nissan Life as a major shareholder, also slid. Nissan Motor Co Ltd lost nine yen to 771.</p>
</text>
